    "version": "4.2.2",
    "scope": "reference",
    "doc_section": "Streams API changes in 2.8.0 (part 1)",
    "content": "We extended `StreamJoined` to include the options `withLoggingEnabled()` and `withLoggingDisabled()` in [KIP-689](https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/x/DyrZCQ). We added two new methods to `KafkaStreams`, namely `KafkaStreams#addStreamThread()` and `KafkaStreams#removeStreamThread()` in [KIP-663](https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/x/FDd4CQ). These methods have enabled adding and removing StreamThreads to a running KafkaStreams client. We deprecated `KafkaStreams#setUncaughtExceptionHandler(fina",
    "source": "https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/4.2.2/docs/streams/upgrade-guide.md",
    "chunk_index": 41,
    "ingested_at": 1793210558.8464272
  }
}
