    "scope": "reference",
    "doc_section": "Remote Authentication > Single Sign-On (SSO) > Configuring the SSO module's appearance",
    "content": "The way a remote authentication backend is displayed to the user on the login\npage may be adjusted via the `SOCIAL_AUTH_BACKEND_ATTRS` parameter, defaulting\nto an empty dictionary. This dictionary maps a `social_core` module's name (ie.\n`REMOTE_AUTH_BACKEND.name`) to a couple of parameters, `(display_name, icon)`.\n\nThe `display_name` is the name displayed to the user on the login page. The\nicon may either be the URL of an icon; refer to a [Material Design\nIcons](https://github.com/google/materia",
    "source": "https://github.com/netbox-community/netbox/blob/v4.7.2/docs/administration/authentication/overview.md",
    "chunk_index": 6,
    "ingested_at": 1793210111.5260255
  }
}
