    "scope": "reference",
    "doc_section": "Dynamic Log Levels",
    "content": "* The dynamic log levels feature allows you to change the log4j settings of a running broker or controller process without restarting it. The command-line syntax for setting dynamic log levels on brokers has not changed in KRaft mode. Here is an example of setting the log level on a broker:\n\n\n        ./bin/kafka-configs.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 \\\n            --entity-type broker-loggers \\\n            --entity-name 1 \\\n            --alter \\\n            --add-config org.apache.kafka.ra",
    "source": "https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/4.2.2/docs/getting-started/zk2kraft.md",
    "chunk_index": 3,
    "ingested_at": 1793210446.172907
  }
